<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Panduvamshis of Dakshina Kosala</h1><p class="st-meta">550 CE – 760 CE (approx.) · capital Shripura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of Chhattisgarh ruling from Sirpur, whose brick Lakshmana temple and Buddhist monasteries are among the treasures of early medieval India.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Panduvamshis, claiming descent from the lunar line, rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakshina-kosala">Dakshina Kosala</a>, the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanadi">Mahanadi</a> valley of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, in the 6th century. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tivaradeva">Tivaradeva</a> they united the region and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirpur-chhattisgarh">Shripura</a>, modern Sirpur, their capital, displacing earlier local rulers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings were mostly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnava</a> but tolerant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahashivagupta-balarjuna">Mahashivagupta Balarjuna</a>, who ruled for about sixty years in the 7th century, was a Shaiva who also endowed Buddhist monasteries; his mother Vasata built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmana-temple-sirpur">Lakshmana temple</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirpur-chhattisgarh">Sirpur</a>, one of the finest early brick temples in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Excavations at Sirpur have revealed monasteries, markets and temples of a thriving city, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> described.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahashivagupta-balarjuna">Balarjuna</a> the dynasty declined in the 8th century. Its line, known as the Somavamshis, moved east into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, where it later ruled as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somavamshi-dynasty">Somavamshi dynasty</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakshina-kosala">Dakshina Kosala</a> passed to other rulers.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 550 CE – 760 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:70.65%;width:4.18%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>550 CE – 760 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shripura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tivaradeva, Mahashivagupta Balarjuna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Panduvamshis of Shripura, Somavamshis of Dakshina Kosala</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=655&amp;focus=panduvamshis-of-dakshina-kosala" aria-label="Panduvamshis of Dakshina Kosala on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6826 1375 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Panduvamshis of Dakshina Kosala lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7146 1631h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7146 1631h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=655&amp;focus=panduvamshis-of-dakshina-kosala">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
